[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991948320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103425#issuecomment-2991948320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103425","id":2991948320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yVYIg","user":{"login":"MichaelDawe","id":75983563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTgzNTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75983563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe","html_url":"https://github.com/MichaelDawe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T15:01:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T15:01:25Z","body":"Just confirming this is still an issue in 4.4.1 and 4.5-beta1.\n\nSystem info:\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 22000) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6590) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400 @ 2.60GHz (12 threads)\n\nAlso it sometimes produces boxy artefacts, at least when used inside a SubViewport.  \n\nI thought this was an issue with SubViewports for ages but they work with FXAA or the new SMAA!\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991948320/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001102660","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103425#issuecomment-3001102660","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103425","id":3001102660,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6y4TFE","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T16:13:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T16:13:27Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/78598 is a partial solution for this problem. We have discussed the full solution a few times. \n\nI think we need an additional subpass after the opaque pass that reads from the depth texture as an input attachment and writes out to a single sample depth texture that can then be sampled from in the transparent pass. \n\nThe approach in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/78598 relies on an extension that is not well supported on mobile GPUs which defeats the purpose since the mobile renderer is intended f